  "_readme": "EMC x TSC1/TSC2, ROUND 7, 2026-08-24 -- the single-copy question, properly this time. Round 5 requested HETLOSS from msk_impact_50k_2026's GISTIC profile and got ZERO records STUDY-WIDE, across all 54,331 samples and every gene. That is not 'no EMC has single-copy loss'; it is proof that THAT PROFILE STORES NO -1 STATE AT ALL. Reading the EMC count alone would have produced exactly the wrong conclusion, which is why the study-wide count was checked. Round 5 also found the right instrument: pancan_pdmr_2025 carries a log2CNA profile -- CONTINUOUS copy number, not a thresholded call -- alongside gistic, and it holds 9 EMC samples. Continuous log2 ratio is what actually answers 'is one copy of TSC2 gone', and no cohort read so far could. Discrete CNA is also requested for the three other cohorts that have a 'cna' profile, with discreteCopyNumberEventType=HETLOSS AND a second call without it, so that an empty payload can again be distinguished from a real zero by comparing the two.",
